Step 2: Add State Management

============================================================

We need to store the image URL using React's useState hook.

import React, { useState } from 'react';

export default function App() {

  const [imageUrl, setImageUrl] = useState('');

  return (
    <div>
      <h2>Random Puppy</h2>

      <button>
        Get Random Puppy
      </button>

      {imageUrl && (
        <img src={imageUrl} alt="Random Puppy" />
      )}
    </div>
  );
}

What Changed?
Code / Item                         | Explanation
------------------------------------|-----------------------------------------
import { useState }                 | Imports the useState hook
useState('')                        | Creates state with an empty initial value
imageUrl                            | Holds the current image URL
setImageUrl                         | Updates the image URL
{imageUrl && <img ... />}           | Displays image only when URL exists

Easy Understanding
imageUrl = empty
      ↓
No image displayed


imageUrl = contains URL
      ↓
Image displayed


This is called Conditional Rendering.

============================================================

Step 3: Create Async Function to Fetch Dog Images

============================================================

Now create the getRandomDog() function.

It fetches an image from the Dog CEO API.

import React, { useState } from 'react';

export default function App() {

  const [imageUrl, setImageUrl] = useState('');
  const [loading, setLoading] = useState(false);

  const getRandomDog = async () => {

    setLoading(true);

    try {

      const response = await fetch(
        'https://dog.ceo/api/breeds/image/random'
      );

      const data = await response.json();

      setImageUrl(data.message);

    } catch (error) {

      console.error('Error fetching dog:', error);

    }

    setLoading(false);
  };

  return (
    <div>

      <h2>Random Puppy</h2>

      <button onClick={getRandomDog}>
        {loading ? 'Loading...' : 'Get Random Puppy'}
      </button>

      {imageUrl && (
        <img src={imageUrl} alt="Random Puppy" />
      )}

    </div>
  );
}

Code Explanation
Code                              | Explanation
----------------------------------|------------------------------------------
useState(false)                   | Creates loading state
getRandomDog = async () => {}     | Creates an asynchronous function
setLoading(true)                  | Marks fetching as started
await fetch(...)                  | Calls API and waits for response
await response.json()             | Converts response to JSON
setImageUrl(data.message)         | Stores returned dog image URL
setLoading(false)                 | Marks fetching as completed
onClick={getRandomDog}            | Calls function when button is clicked
loading ? 'Loading...' : ...      | Changes button text while loading


